<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<set xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shareInterpolator="false">
    <!-- CLOSE-exit of the platform's custom cross-Activity back animation, and the
         closing window's exit animation for a plain toolbar/back-button finish.

         Why this file carries the whole exit:
         CustomCrossActivityBackAnimation never advances currentClosingRect after the
         gesture is committed. It keeps the rect the finger released on and applies only
         this animation's alpha and matrix, then removes the window when
         getPostCommitAnimationDuration() expires. An identity alpha therefore left the
         closing page standing still at the release position until its leash was removed,
         which is the hard pop this pair must not reintroduce.

         Both children run on the full post-commit clock and differ only by interpolator.
         That is deliberate: AnimationSet.getTransformationAt() (used by the Shell)
         forwards the raw 0..1 progress to every child without renormalising by the
         child's duration or startOffset, so a shorter child would simply be evaluated
         past its end (Animation.getTransformationAt does not clamp either). Giving both
         children duration == the set duration keeps the Shell's progress-driven mapping
         and the normal time-driven window transition (toolbar back) in agreement.

         Shape:
         - alpha 1 -> 0 with oxygen_classic_page_back_alpha: the alpha is fully gone at
           ~26% of the post-commit progress (~117 ms of 450 ms). The real parent page
           is already fully composed underneath, so any foreground alpha left after the
           first fifth of the clock reads as a double-exposed text/list ghost. A plain
           built-in interpolator cannot express that: decelerate_quad still leaves 56%
           opacity at progress 0.25 and 42% at 0.35. The platform reference,
           DefaultCrossActivityBackAnimation, fades the closing page out completely at
           20%; the tail of this curve is deliberately slightly softer than that.
         - translate 0 -> 96dp, fast_out_slow_in (the XML approximation of the Shell's
           EMPHASIZED curve). 96dp is DefaultCrossActivityBackAnimation's
           cross_activity_back_entering_start_offset; on commit it retargets the closing
           rect to currentClosingRect.left + 96dp. +X is correct for *both* swipe edges:
           the pre-commit phase already owns left/right direction and the post-commit
           target is always the release position moved further along +X.
         Do not add scale or rotation: the Shell composes this matrix under its own scale
         and crop, so extra geometry would fight it. -->
    <alpha
        android:fromAlpha="1.0"
        android:toAlpha="0.0"
        android:interpolator="@interpolator/oxygen_classic_page_back_alpha"
        android:startOffset="0"
        android:duration="@integer/oxygen_classic_page_back_duration_ms" />

    <translate
        android:fromXDelta="0"
        android:toXDelta="@dimen/oxygen_classic_page_back_slide_distance"
        android:interpolator="@android:interpolator/fast_out_slow_in"
        android:startOffset="0"
        android:duration="@integer/oxygen_classic_page_back_duration_ms" />
</set>
